# Instance-owned files: framework tag-merges never overwrite these.
# Git uses the "ours" merge strategy for any merge (including `git merge <tag>`),
# keeping this instance's version and discarding the incoming framework change.
#
# REQUIRED once per clone (not version-controlled, so it cannot ship here):
#   git config merge.ours.driver true
# The `ours` driver is not built into git; without that config line every
# `merge=ours` below silently no-ops. `/sekai-upgrade` and
# docs/runbook/UPGRADE.md set it.
#
# This is instance #1 (lagunabeach.md), re-based onto the sekai-kb framework in
# task 5.4. ADR 006 approved the full instance-owned list below: place.config.ts,
# knowledge/**, public/media/**, CNAME, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, README.md, CHANGELOG.md,
# VERSION, FRAMEWORK-VERSION,
# docs/baselines/**, scripts/ci/genericity-denylist.local.txt, and
# .agent-toolkit/**. ADR 008 (in sekai-kb) adds the four planning-document paths:
# docs/PRD.md, docs/SPEC.md, docs/ROADMAP.md, and docs/adr/**.
# See docs/runbook/UPGRADE.md §Instance-owned files. Add your own below.

place.config.ts merge=ours
knowledge/** merge=ours
public/media/** merge=ours
CNAME merge=ours
CLAUDE.md merge=ours
AGENTS.md merge=ours
README.md merge=ours
CHANGELOG.md merge=ours
VERSION merge=ours
FRAMEWORK-VERSION merge=ours
docs/baselines/** merge=ours
scripts/ci/genericity-denylist.local.txt merge=ours

# Dev-plugin state (agent-toolkit): the config + promoted rules are committed and
# instance-owned — this instance carries its OWN .agent-toolkit/, so a framework
# tag-merge must never overwrite it with the framework's own dev config or rules.
.agent-toolkit/** merge=ours

# Maintainer-doc paths (ADR 008). The init wizard strips the framework's own copies,
# so most instances have nothing here and these lines are inert. An instance that
# keeps its OWN product, architecture, delivery, or decision records at these paths
# is a legitimate state, and its documents are never the framework's to overwrite —
# shipping the attribute means such an instance is protected by default instead of
# having to remember to add it before its next merge. Absence is a different problem
# that no attribute can solve; scripts/upgrade/maintainer-docs-state.mjs owns it.
docs/PRD.md merge=ours
docs/SPEC.md merge=ours
docs/ROADMAP.md merge=ours
docs/adr/** merge=ours
